    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.full_join - EdgeCase\", \"isPartOf\":\n    {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.full_join.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.full_join()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: >-\n    Join this graph with another, linking every node of one to every node of the\n    other.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.full_join()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: >-\n    Join this graph with another, linking every node of one to every node of the\n    other.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.full_join()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: >-\n  Join this graph with another, linking every node of one to every node of the\n  other.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nJoin this graph with another, linking every node of one to every node of the other.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L52409-L52518){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.full_join(other)\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![Full join](../assets/graphs/full-join.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"G is a 5-cycle on nodes 1 to 5 and H is a single node, hub (teal). The full join keeps both graphs and adds an accent edge from every node of G to every node of H: five spokes from the hub to the rim. The result is a wheel with 6 nodes and 10 edges, and hub has degree 5.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nThe full join (graph join) $G + H$ is the disjoint union of the two graphs plus an edge\nbetween every node of this graph and every node of `other` (in both directions for\ndirected graphs). Joins build classic families from small pieces: a wheel is a cycle\njoined with a single hub, a complete bipartite graph is the join of two edgeless graphs,\nand a cone over any graph is its join with one node. They also model two groups with\nall-to-all contact between them, such as two departments in a fully connected meeting.\n\nThe two graphs must have the same directedness. Node IDs and labels follow\n`disjoint_union()`: this graph's nodes keep their IDs, `other`'s are shifted above them,\nand clashing labels get a numeric suffix.\n:::\n\n## Parameters {.doc-parameters}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code>[other]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Graph]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   The graph to join. Neither graph is modified.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [Graph]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   A new graph with all nodes and edges of both graphs plus the `n * m` joining edges\n    (`2 * n * m` if directed). Joining edges carry no weight or attributes.\n:::\n\n## Raises {.doc-raises}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [ValueError]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If the graphs have different directedness.\n:::\n\n## Technical Notes {.doc-technical-notes}\n\nBuilt as `disjoint_union()` followed by the cross edges, in $O(V + E + nm)$ time.\nNetworkX's `full_join` requires disjoint node names (or a `rename=` prefix); EdgeCase\nrenumbers automatically.\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~disjoint_union`) \n\n:   Combine two graphs, keeping their nodes apart.\n\n[](`~corona_product`) \n\n:   Join each node to its own copy of another graph.\n\n[](`~add_complete_bipartite_graph`) \n\n:   Add a complete bipartite graph.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nA full join is a disjoint union plus an edge from every node of one graph to every node of\nthe other. Joining a 5-cycle to a single hub gives a wheel:\n\n::: {#9ea2ccb3 .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\nrim = ec.Graph().add_cycle_graph(5)\nhub = ec.Graph().add_nodes([\"hub\"])\n\nwheel = rim.full_join(hub)\nwheel.count_edges(), wheel.get_degree(\"hub\")\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\n(10, 5)\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### A coach for the climbers\n\n`ec.friends()` is a network of friendships among the members of a chess club and a climbing\nclub. The climbing club's 12 members have 18 friendships among them. A new coach who\nbefriends every climber is a full join with a one-node graph, which adds 12 edges:\n\n::: {#aa6f6555 .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nfriends = ec.friends()\nnodes = friends.get_node_df()\nclimbers = nodes.filter(club=\"Climbing\")[\"id\"].to_list()\n\nclimbing = friends.subgraph(climbers)\ncoach = ec.Graph().add_nodes([\"Coach\"])\n\nteam = climbing.full_join(coach)\nteam.count_edges(), team.get_degree(\"Coach\")\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```\n(30, 12)\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n::: {#c168152f .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\ncoach_id = team.get_id_from_label(\"Coach\")\n\nteam.plot(\n    label_by=\"label\", highlight=[\"Coach\"], seed=1,\n    highlight_edges=[(coach_id, n) for n in team.get_neighbors(coach_id)],\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-b9f8de6d:#872d08;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-b9f8de6d:#ae500f;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}}:is(html.quarto-light, body.quarto-light, html[data-bs-theme=\"light\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"true\"], body.vscode-light, body.vscode-high-contrast-light, html[theme=\"light\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-b9f8de6d:#872d08;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}:is(html.quarto-dark, body.quarto-dark, html[data-bs-theme=\"dark\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"false\"], body.vscode-dark, body.vscode-high-contrast:not(.vscode-high-contrast-light), html[theme=\"dark\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-b9f8de6d:#ae500f;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}</style><div class=\"ec-plot\" style=\"position:relative;width:fit-content;max-width:100%;margin:1em auto\">\n<style>.ec-plot > svg { display:block; max-width:100%; height:auto; }</style>\n<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"700\" height=\"500\" viewBox=\"5.6 14.0 688.8 492.0\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif;\">\n<rect x=\"5.6\" y=\"14.0\" width=\"688.8\" height=\"492.0\" fill=\"var(--ect-3239c383)\"/>\n<line x1=\"530.9\" y1=\"301.7\" x2=\"555.1\" y2=\"267.3\" stroke=\"var(--ect-